{
  "slug": "velixar",
  "name": "Velixar",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Velixar is a cognitive memory system for Claude Code. It gives Claude persistent memory, a knowledge graph, identity awareness, contradiction detection, and belief tracking across every session, not just\nsession logs, but a full reasoning layer.\n\n6 skills, 1 agent, 40 MCP tools, 5 live resources, and 18 workflow prompts. Claude doesn't just remember what you said, it understands how your decisions evolved, detects when new information contradicts stored knowledge, and maintains a persistent model of who you are and how you work.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **6 skills**, **1 agent**, **1 hook** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (6): `velixar-contradict` (Detect contradictions between current information and stored memories), `velixar-recall` (Search persistent memory for relevant context), `velixar-reflect` (Generate a cognitive briefing for the current session), `velixar-remember` (Store important context in persistent memory), `velixar-session` (Consolidate the current session into persistent memory), `velixar-setup` (Set up Velixar persistent memory for this Claude Code session)\n- **Agents** (1): `velixar-librarian` (A memory librarian agent that organizes, deduplicates, and curates stored memories)\n- **Hooks** (1): `Stop`\n- **MCP servers** (1): `velixar`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install velixar@claude-community` from `VelixarAi/velixar-claude-plugin`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 6,
    "agent": 1,
    "hook": 1,
    "mcp": 1
  },
